// MAIN ENTRY POINT FOR SELF-HOSTED SOUNIO COMPILER
// Horizon 2 (step 1): main.sio uses `use` imports from lexer.
// Deeper module wiring (module_loader, typecheck, gen) is done incrementally
// as each module gains its own `use` imports.
//
// Usage: souc input.sio [-o output] [-t target] [-O] [-v] [--emit-tokens]

// Horizon 3: wire to real multi-module native compilation pipeline
// Restore the broader modular baseline imports first; we can narrow these again
// once the uncapped main.sio lane is type-stable.
